.\" mkz.1: manual page for the pure-C mkz.
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
.Dd June 29, 2026
.Dt MKZ 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mkz
.Nd reversible columnar pre-pass + zstd archiver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl c
.Op Fl z Ns Ar level
.Op Fl v
.Fl f Ar archive
.Ar file ...
.Nm
.Fl x
.Op Fl v
.Fl f Ar archive
.Op Ar destdir
.Nm
.Op Fl hV
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a tar-style archiver whose backend is a reversible, schema-free
.Em auto-columnar
transform followed by
.Xr zstd 1 .
It is not a new compressor but a structural pre-pass that makes a general
compressor smaller on structured, line-oriented data
.Pq logs, CSV, JSONL, telemetry
and never worse anywhere else.
.Pp
For each block of input,
.Nm
discovers record structure with no schema, gathers the varying fields into
per-column streams, delta-codes numeric columns, and dedups repeated values
through a shared dictionary, producing a packed blob.
It then compresses both the raw block and the transformed blob with
.Xr zstd 1
and keeps whichever is smaller
.Pq the never-worse gate ,
so the transform can only help or no-op.
Every archive carries a SHA-256 of the reconstructed original; extraction
verifies this SHA-256 over the whole stream and reports corruption on a
mismatch.
Extraction is atomic: entries are staged under a
.Pa .mkz-partial. Ns Ar pid
directory inside
.Ar destdir
and are placed into
.Ar destdir
only after the SHA-256 trailer verifies.
A failed extraction places nothing in
.Ar destdir ;
the staging directory is left in place for inspection.
.Pp
Both creation and extraction stream line-oriented input in bounded memory for
typical text and logs: peak memory is roughly one block.
Only one input file is open at a time.
Pathological newline-free input is the exception: a block is read up to the
next newline, so a file with no newlines is buffered whole and is not yet
bounded.
.Pp
This is the pure-C build; it is byte-compatible with the reference
implementation in both directions.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Create an archive from the given files and directories.
.It Fl x
Extract an archive.
The optional
.Ar destdir
defaults to the current directory.
.It Fl z Ns Ar level
Set the
.Xr zstd 1
compression level
.Pq 1 to 22, default 12 .
The level attaches to the flag with no space and may be clustered with
.Fl c ,
e.g.\&
.Fl cz19f .
.It Fl f Ar archive
The archive file to create or read
.Pq required .
.It Fl v
Verbose: list each entry as it is processed.
.It Fl h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PSRC_AC_ZSTD_LEVEL
.It Ev PSRC_AC_ZSTD_LEVEL
Default
.Xr zstd 1
level when
.Cm z
is not given
.Pq default 12 .
.It Ev PSRC_AC_BLOCK_MB
Block size in mebibytes for create
.Pq default 16 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
On extract,
.Nm
fails
.Pq nonzero
if the archive is malformed, truncated, or fails its SHA-256 integrity check.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a compressed archive of
.Pa /var/log :
.Pp
.Dl $ mkz -czf logs.mkz /var/log
.Pp
Create at
.Xr zstd 1
level 19, verbosely:
.Pp
.Dl $ mkz -cz19vf data.mkz data/
.Pp
Extract into
.Pa out/ :
.Pp
.Dl $ mkz -xvf logs.mkz out/
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tar 1 ,
.Xr zstd 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The archive format is the
.Sy PAS1
container: a magic, a sequence of framed
.Xr zstd 1
blocks
.Pq each flagged raw or auto-columnar ,
and a trailing SHA-256 of the reconstructed original.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Matthew Klein .
.Sh CAVEATS
Extract requires a seekable archive file;
.Cm mkz -xf -
(stdin) is refused with an explanatory error.
.Pp
Symbolic links and special files are skipped.
Stored paths are normalized to be relocatable; extraction rejects absolute
paths and
.Sq ..
traversal.
